              "text": "For the **2026 NBA Playoffs**, the Indiana Pacers did **not qualify**. Ravaged by injuries\u2014most notably losing star guard Tyrese Haliburton for the entire season due to a torn Achilles tendon sustained in the 2025 Finals\u2014the Pacers finished the 2025\u201326 regular season with a 19\u201363 record and were the first team eliminated from postseason contention. \n\nHowever, looking back at their most recent playoff appearances:\n\n### **2025 NBA Playoffs (Run to the NBA Finals)**\nIn 2025, the Pacers had a historic run all the way to the NBA Finals as the 4th seed:\n*   **First Round:** Defeated the **Milwaukee Bucks** (4\u20131)\n*   **Eastern Conference Semifinals:** Defeated the **Cleveland Cavaliers** (4\u20131)\n*   **Eastern Conference Finals:** Defeated the **New York Knicks** (4\u20132)\n*   **NBA Finals:** Lost to the **Oklahoma City Thunder** (3\u20134) in a hard-fought seven-game series.\n\n### **2024 NBA Playoffs (Run to the Eastern Conference Finals)**\nIn 2024, the Pacers made an unexpected push deep into the postseason:\n*   **First Round:** Defeated the **Milwaukee Bucks** (4\u20132)\n*   **Eastern Conference Semifinals:** Defeated the **New York Knicks** (4\u20133)\n*   **Eastern Conference Finals:** Lost to the **Boston Celtics** (0\u20134)",
